infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title When external beats context — same write-heavy load
  desc Each side has a mechanism, not a fashion: who gets notified per write decides the cost
  compares
    - label Context
      children
        - label Notifies every consumer per write
          desc No selectors — any change to the value's identity re-renders all consumers, full stop
        - label ~1,000 renders/sec under load
          desc 20 writes/sec across 50 consumers = every consumer re-renders on every tick
        - label Needs the provider in the tree
          desc Consumers must live under the provider; no read from event handlers or non-React code
        - label Wins for low-write, scoped values
          desc Theme, locale, current user — the provider hierarchy is the feature
    - label External store
      children
        - label Re-renders only matching selectors
          desc Each component declares its slice; Object.is on selector output, shallow equality opt-in
        - label A handful of renders for the same load
          desc A promo-code write re-renders zero components that only selected items.length
        - label Module singleton — no provider
          desc Importable cross-tree: event handlers, route loaders, analytics, non-React code
        - label Store-boundary tooling
          desc persist, immer, devtools action history attach at the store boundary
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
